_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 35
---
order: 35
---
short_label: IX.35
---
statement: If as many numbers as we please are in continued proportion, and there is subtracted from the second and the last numbers equal to the first, then the excess of the second is to the first as the excess of the last is to the sum of all those before it.
---
proof:

---
body:

